OL,3,GNEWSAWhat is life really like working
OL,4,Ain the aviation industry?
OL,5,
OL,6,FPete Smith always secures the best seat
OL,7,Fon the plane.
OL,9,F"No matter the time of year, we always
OL,10,Fget some sunshine when we go to work,"
OL,11,Fsaid Capt Smith, who has worked in the
OL,12,Faviation industry for 30 years after
OL,13,Fdeciding to pursue his dreams following
OL,14,Fa decade working for British Gas.
OL,16,F"It's a fantastic office, there's worse
OL,17,Fplaces to work."
OL,19,FBank holiday weekends can be even
OL,20,Fbusier for pilots and cabin crews, with
OL,21,FSmith's alarm clock going off at 03:30
OL,22,FBST for a flight to Croatia.
